    mantic:parable "Ogbe rises first — light at its first opening — and sets the stage of beginnings, clarity, the uncarried day. Over it walks Osa, the storm that assembles: Rises and extends, the reading now disperses then collects. The danger here is light that ignores the shadow exhausts itself by noon; the working gift is what scatters you also spreads your name. \"However long the night, the dawn arrives without knocking. Yet the storm rearranges the furniture before the feast.\"" ;
