    mantic:parable "Ogbe rises first — light at its first opening — and sets the stage of beginnings, clarity, the uncarried day. Over it walks Oturupon, the long-walking elder: Rises and extends, the reading now endures and ripens. The danger here is light that ignores the shadow exhausts itself by noon; the working gift is outlasting the thing that tested you. \"However long the night, the dawn arrives without knocking. Yet patience is the only horse that finishes the race.\"" ;
