    mantic:hasBinaryVector "11111011" ;
    mantic:leftLeg "Ogbe" ;
    mantic:parable "Ogbe rises first — light at its first opening — and sets the stage of beginnings, clarity, the uncarried day. Over it walks Irete, the closed fist of order: Rises and extends, the reading now grips and orders. The danger here is light that ignores the shadow exhausts itself by noon; the working gift is the will that finishes the sentence. \"However long the night, the dawn arrives without knocking. Yet the matter ends where the will stands firm.\"" ;
    mantic:rightLeg "Irete" .

mantic:Odu015 a mantic:IfaOdu ;
    rdfs:label "Ogbe-Ose" ;
    mantic:figureIndex 15 ;
    mantic:hasBinaryVector "11110001" ;
    mantic:leftLeg "Ogbe" ;
    mantic:parable "Ogbe rises first — light at its first opening — and sets the stage of beginnings, clarity, the uncarried day. Over it walks Ose, the blessing that outruns you: Rises and extends, the reading now arrives like weather. The danger here is light that ignores the shadow exhausts itself by noon; the working gift is winning without needing to win. \"However long the night, the dawn arrives without knocking. Yet the harvest answers the name of the patient farmer.\"" ;
    mantic:rightLeg "Ose" .

mantic:Odu016 a mantic:IfaOdu ;
    rdfs:label "Ogbe-Ofun" ;
    mantic:figureIndex 16 ;
    mantic:hasBinaryVector "11111000" ;
    mantic:leftLeg "Ogbe" ;
    mantic:parable "Ogbe rises first — light at its first opening — and sets the stage of beginnings, clarity, the uncarried day. Over it walks Ofun, the long white road: Rises and extends, the reading now extends and teaches. The danger here is light that ignores the shadow exhausts itself by noon; the working gift is the long view that shortens the road. \"However long the night, the dawn arrives without knocking. Yet the elder's word outruns the young man's horse.\"" ;
    mantic:rightLeg "Ofun" .

mantic:Odu017 a mantic:IfaOdu ;
    rdfs:label "Oyeku-Ogbe" ;
    mantic:figureIndex 17 ;
    mantic:hasBinaryVector "00001111" ;
    mantic:leftLeg "Oyeku" ;
    mantic:parable "Oyeku rises first — the closing gate — and sets the stage of endings, ancestors, the fertile dark. Over it walks Ogbe, light at its first opening: Withdraws and gathers, the reading now rises and extends. The danger here is staying past the ending rots the granary; the working gift is a clean start granted, not earned. \"The elder who greets the ancestors first eats the fattest yam. Yet light renews its contract every morning.\"" ;
    mantic:rightLeg "Ogbe" .

